Parent companion for FPGA-gPTP #84 in the physical-rate milan_dp_gptp suite
(tb/verilator/milan_dp/sim_ax1x1gptp.cpp). Rides the same gptp-processor pin
adoption. Apply after parent-adoption-milan_dp-82.patch:
git apply parent-adoption-milan_dp_gptp-84.patch

#84: a grandmaster's own time is the domain's time (IEEE 1722-2016 4.4.4.7
and 10.4; Milan v1.2 4.3.5.2), so while this station is grandmaster the
published sync-ok is set and tu is clear, except during the Milan v1.2 Annex
B.1.1 holdover that a grandmaster change arms (the parent holds HOLD_QTICK_P =
2 quarter-ticks, 0.25 s to 0.5 s). In the loss arm the Announce receipt
timeout makes this station grandmaster, so the harness's assumptions that a
lost peer leaves tu set, and that CLKV "healthy" implies the peer is elected,
no longer hold.

| Line | Expectation | Was | Now |
|---|---|---|---|
| 344 | Until conditions | - | adds SelfGm (public GM is thisClock) and GmCertain (sync set, tu clear) |
| 1015 | Until::Healthy | asCapable, sync, no tu, two answers | the same, and the public GM is the peer's (kGm) |
| 1018 | Until::PeerLost | asCapable, sync and tu read 0x1 after four unanswered intervals | asCapable clear after four unanswered intervals (the role no longer matters) |
| 1055 | peer-loss window, AAF tu required 1 for the whole 4.6 s | one window, tu 1 | three windows: tu 1 until this station is grandmaster; the holdover (transition, not compared); tu 0 until the fourth missed Pdelay |
| new | the grandmaster change holds tu for the 0.25 s holdover | - | >= 0.25 s less the 4 ms polling margin |
| new | tu clears within 0.5 s of the grandmaster change | - | sync set, tu clear, <= 0.5 s plus 4 ms |
| 948 | publication "lost": sync and tu | 0x1 ("loss clears Sync and asserts uncertainty") | 0x2 ("the grandmaster role is synchronised, uncertainty cleared") |
| new | publication "lost": the grandmaster | - | kThisClock ("loss leaves this station grandmaster") |

The extended mode (make extended) keeps one peer-loss window, marked as a
transition (tu not compared), because its fixed 4.6 s span crosses the
grandmaster change.

